A||||4||btoth||quick tach question||||5||
Z||000000||btoth||07-26-2000||04:53 PM||||ok.. all of a sudden today my tach started jumping all over the place when i hit the gas (this only would happen when in 1st gear for some reason - btw:  it's an automatic).  while the tach is jumping, the car stutter's a lot... is this a common symptom of a bad tach filter? or is it something more serious?  thanx in advance.   ~ brian.||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfixit58||07-26-2000||05:02 PM||||sounds like a bad tach filter. See Rodney:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/tachfilter.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/tachfilter.htm</A> <P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||286SE'S||07-26-2000||05:36 PM||||Disconnect the tach filter and see if your engine runs smoothly. If not it may be the ignition module in the distributor, it drives the tach as part of its function.<BR>Terry||||reg||1
Z||000003||batboy||07-26-2000||06:42 PM||||Lots of things can cause that. The tach filter is one place to check. Lots of ignition problems can do it too. My 85 GT started doing that when started cold and quit after it warmed up. It turned out to be a fried distributor cap and rotor.||||reg||1
Z||000004||btoth||07-26-2000||11:02 PM||||well... i found the problems...  the wires for my coil were loose (don't know how that happened).  and my tach filter is messed up... when i plug it in my car stalls so i have it disconected.  does anyone know what makes this happen?  does the tach filter have anything to do with the car's computer?  thanx.||||reg||1
